1
00:00:48,840 --> 00:00:50,175
Looks like we can't get out of here.

2
00:00:50,258 --> 00:00:51,885
We still have one option.

3
00:00:51,968 --> 00:00:54,095
You really trust that informant that much.

4
00:00:54,179 --> 00:00:56,139
- He's here.
- Hi!

5
00:00:56,222 --> 00:00:59,017
Rahmboy, the area is on lockdown.

6
00:00:59,100 --> 00:01:00,143
No one's getting out.

7
00:01:00,226 --> 00:01:01,811
Where are you planning to hide us?

8
00:01:01,895 --> 00:01:04,773
Worse than an animal cage or a sewer, bro.

9
00:01:04,856 --> 00:01:06,399
Where? Why here?

10
00:01:06,483 --> 00:01:09,235
<i>The mafia is not allowed to operate there.</i>

11
00:01:09,319 --> 00:01:12,489
The Castellanis won't make a move
inside that five-star hotel.

12
00:01:14,741 --> 00:01:16,159
Why haven't we heard anything on comms?

13
00:01:16,242 --> 00:01:17,243
What's happening to Alex?

14
00:01:17,327 --> 00:01:19,162
They're safe, but they are compromised.

15
00:01:19,245 --> 00:01:20,371
We don't need to go there.

16
00:01:20,455 --> 00:01:23,792
We have Mikoy's asset there
who can help them.

17
00:01:42,018 --> 00:01:43,228
They found us. We need to move!

18
00:01:43,895 --> 00:01:45,313
Come on!

19
00:01:48,650 --> 00:01:50,276
I saw her. Chiara.

20
00:01:50,360 --> 00:01:53,279
Looks like she's coming back
to the Philippines.

21
00:01:56,491 --> 00:01:59,202
And as for the question
of whether we can trust him, yes.

22
00:01:59,285 --> 00:02:00,995
Mikoy's asset can be trusted.

23
00:02:02,330 --> 00:02:05,500
Mom! This is for you! Fresh from Italy.

24
00:02:05,583 --> 00:02:07,210
Can I talk to you?

25
00:02:13,383 --> 00:02:14,425
Here’s my gift.

26
00:02:25,103 --> 00:02:26,563
That should come in handy

27
00:02:27,313 --> 00:02:30,483
if you want to slice Mikoy’s neck.

28
00:02:41,327 --> 00:02:42,579
Seriously?

29
00:02:42,662 --> 00:02:44,205
Fresh from Italy.

30
00:02:45,915 --> 00:02:49,711
Come on, I could even buy that
at my favorite grocery store.

31
00:02:54,257 --> 00:02:55,633
Sorry, Mom.

32
00:02:56,134 --> 00:02:58,761
My schedule in Italy was just too tight,

33
00:02:58,845 --> 00:03:00,763
so I didn't get to buy any gifts.

34
00:03:02,056 --> 00:03:05,226
You know those crazies.
They're like cough syrup.

35
00:03:05,310 --> 00:03:06,978
They just found out I'm going abroad,

36
00:03:07,061 --> 00:03:09,480
and they already expect gifts.

37
00:03:11,482 --> 00:03:13,401
What were you really doing there?

38
00:03:17,322 --> 00:03:18,406
It's nothing, Mom.

39
00:03:18,489 --> 00:03:21,284
It was just for the tourism.

40
00:03:23,786 --> 00:03:25,997
Hey, Mikoy. Come on.

41
00:03:26,080 --> 00:03:28,708
Stop lying to me.

42
00:03:28,791 --> 00:03:32,378
I'm your mother,
and just by looking at you,

43
00:03:32,462 --> 00:03:35,215
I know when you're not telling the truth.

44
00:03:35,715 --> 00:03:38,176
You know, if your father were here,

45
00:03:38,259 --> 00:03:40,220
he'd be ashamed of you.

46
00:03:40,803 --> 00:03:44,265
Come to think of it,
you're lying to your own mother.

47
00:03:49,604 --> 00:03:52,190
Fine. So I won't have to lie anymore.

48
00:03:53,316 --> 00:03:54,859
Just don't ask me about it, Mom.

49
00:03:55,360 --> 00:03:56,861
I just had something to take care of.

50
00:03:58,321 --> 00:03:59,322
Chiara?

51
00:04:00,240 --> 00:04:01,532
Did you talk to Chiara?

52
00:04:06,079 --> 00:04:09,249
There's another reason
why you want Mikoy gone so badly.

53
00:04:10,667 --> 00:04:11,751
Like what?

54
00:04:15,755 --> 00:04:18,007
But you think I still love him.

55
00:04:19,008 --> 00:04:22,011
You think that if we see each other again,

56
00:04:22,095 --> 00:04:23,554
if we talk,

57
00:04:24,055 --> 00:04:27,684
there's a chance
that he could change my mind and heart.

58
00:04:32,480 --> 00:04:34,023
That's not true!

59
00:04:34,107 --> 00:04:35,441
But it is.

60
00:04:37,026 --> 00:04:38,945
That's why Mikoy is a threat to you.

61
00:04:39,445 --> 00:04:40,405
Because you know that

62
00:04:40,488 --> 00:04:43,491
if there's one person
in this world I'd listen to, it's him.

63
00:04:44,659 --> 00:04:47,745
After all, we have
a deep history together.

64
00:04:51,833 --> 00:04:53,167
Wait a minute.

65
00:04:53,251 --> 00:04:55,503
Did you talk to her as Mikoy

66
00:04:55,586 --> 00:04:57,964
or as a member of GAGO?

67
00:04:58,047 --> 00:04:59,382
A police asset?

68
00:05:00,633 --> 00:05:01,467
Mom.

69
00:05:02,218 --> 00:05:05,054
Don't pull the "Mom" card on me!

70
00:05:05,972 --> 00:05:07,807
Answer my question!

71
00:05:07,890 --> 00:05:10,226
What's going on with you?

72
00:05:11,894 --> 00:05:14,147
Did you do something wrong

73
00:05:14,647 --> 00:05:16,649
because of what happened to your father?

74
00:05:16,733 --> 00:05:18,192
Son,

75
00:05:19,360 --> 00:05:22,613
did you take the law into your own hands?

76
00:05:24,490 --> 00:05:25,658
No, Mom.

77
00:05:27,660 --> 00:05:29,245
Oh, son.

78
00:05:30,038 --> 00:05:31,914
Just stop this.

79
00:05:33,291 --> 00:05:37,295
This won't end well, believe me.

80
00:05:39,672 --> 00:05:42,008
Just learn to forgive.

81
00:05:42,508 --> 00:05:44,010
To understand.

82
00:05:48,139 --> 00:05:49,515
It still hurts, son.

83
00:05:51,434 --> 00:05:54,479
Even I'm still
completely broken to this day.

84
00:05:55,396 --> 00:05:56,230
You know that.

85
00:05:58,983 --> 00:06:00,109
But our pain

86
00:06:00,693 --> 00:06:03,237
shouldn't dictates

87
00:06:03,821 --> 00:06:06,866
how we live,

88
00:06:07,366 --> 00:06:09,535
on how we make our decisions.

89
00:06:13,498 --> 00:06:15,917
You know, that pain won't go away.

90
00:06:18,419 --> 00:06:19,670
Even your father,

91
00:06:20,463 --> 00:06:21,881
he wouldn't want this.

92
00:06:24,008 --> 00:06:28,137
Even me, as your mother,
I don't want this to be the life you live.

93
00:06:46,322 --> 00:06:48,449
And you think

94
00:06:48,533 --> 00:06:51,661
you can make me obey you
because I'm under your spell.

95
00:06:52,286 --> 00:06:53,204
But I'm not.

96
00:06:58,334 --> 00:07:01,796
So don't ever think
that you're the hero of this story.

97
00:07:02,505 --> 00:07:03,965
Because anytime…

98
00:07:12,098 --> 00:07:15,017
So if you want to keep existing,

99
00:07:15,893 --> 00:07:19,397
never, ever tell me
what I can and cannot do.

100
00:07:21,774 --> 00:07:23,151
And most of all,

101
00:07:23,734 --> 00:07:25,278
you have no right

102
00:07:25,361 --> 00:07:28,239
to dictate who I should keep alive

103
00:07:28,322 --> 00:07:30,116
or who I should kill.

104
00:07:36,914 --> 00:07:39,041
I believe it'll come in handy

105
00:07:39,125 --> 00:07:40,710
when I want to slit the throat of someone

106
00:07:41,794 --> 00:07:42,962
who gets on my nerves.

107
00:08:07,069 --> 00:08:08,279
<i>For Mario?</i>

108
00:08:08,779 --> 00:08:11,157
<i>Are you going to avenge your father?</i>

109
00:08:12,700 --> 00:08:13,534
<i>Dad.</i>

110
00:08:21,501 --> 00:08:23,002
<i>But it shouldn't be</i>

111
00:08:23,503 --> 00:08:25,796
<i>that the pain we're feeling</i>

112
00:08:25,880 --> 00:08:29,342
- Dad!
- <i>dictates how we live our lives.</i>

113
00:08:31,302 --> 00:08:33,179
<i>How we make our decisions.</i>

114
00:08:33,262 --> 00:08:35,264
Dad. Dad!

115
00:08:39,685 --> 00:08:42,230
<i>Mom, I'm really sorry.</i>
<i>Dad, I'm really sorry.</i>

116
00:08:42,730 --> 00:08:44,690
<i>If this all happened because of me.</i>

117
00:08:44,774 --> 00:08:48,110
<i>But I have to do what I believe is right.</i>

118
00:09:03,668 --> 00:09:05,127
What is it again?!

119
00:11:20,805 --> 00:11:22,264
You're going to have Chiara killed?

120
00:11:30,481 --> 00:11:33,484
You heard what the Concordat said.

121
00:11:34,110 --> 00:11:37,822
They're getting nervous,
and they're running out of patience.

122
00:11:38,697 --> 00:11:41,700
Chiara wasn't even supposed
to come home to the Philippines

123
00:11:41,784 --> 00:11:43,869
to meet Mikoy.

124
00:11:45,621 --> 00:11:47,456
Chiara has become unpredictable.

125
00:11:48,749 --> 00:11:52,169
We need to act now to protect

126
00:11:52,253 --> 00:11:54,130
our position!

127
00:11:54,213 --> 00:11:55,798
So you're just going
to turn your back on Chiara?

128
00:11:57,716 --> 00:12:00,845
Maybe we're being too hasty
with our decisions, Mom.

129
00:12:02,346 --> 00:12:03,180
Son,

130
00:12:03,681 --> 00:12:05,641
Chiara already made her choice

131
00:12:06,559 --> 00:12:08,769
when she met with Mikoy.

132
00:12:09,478 --> 00:12:12,022
She still hasn't moved on.

133
00:12:13,816 --> 00:12:17,736
She had the opportunity
to have Mikoy killed in Italy,

134
00:12:17,820 --> 00:12:19,196
but she couldn't do it.

135
00:12:20,030 --> 00:12:24,118
Which means she still
has feelings for Mikoy.

136
00:12:24,201 --> 00:12:26,996
And that will ruin our plans.

137
00:12:27,079 --> 00:12:28,247
- But Mom--
- Son.

138
00:12:37,214 --> 00:12:39,341
I treated her like my own daughter.

139
00:12:40,384 --> 00:12:41,760
I raised her

140
00:12:41,844 --> 00:12:43,554
like she was my own child.

141
00:12:44,889 --> 00:12:46,599
But just like Donatello,

142
00:12:46,682 --> 00:12:48,142
what they did?

143
00:12:48,225 --> 00:12:49,935
They refuse to obey me.

144
00:12:50,436 --> 00:12:52,146
They refuse to listen to me.

145
00:12:56,150 --> 00:12:58,486
It's too late for your Sister Chiara.

146
00:13:00,112 --> 00:13:01,614
Let's think about

147
00:13:02,907 --> 00:13:04,992
what's best for the two of us.

148
00:13:05,659 --> 00:13:07,578
I'm doing this for you.

149
00:13:08,621 --> 00:13:09,622
For you, son.

150
00:13:11,081 --> 00:13:13,334
Because I don't want you
to end up like me.

151
00:13:14,293 --> 00:13:17,963
Trampled on and treated
like you were nothing by others.

152
00:13:18,047 --> 00:13:19,048
Mom.

153
00:13:26,931 --> 00:13:28,182
I can't do it.

154
00:13:30,893 --> 00:13:32,019
You don't have to.

155
00:13:34,230 --> 00:13:36,690
I know you can't
bring yourself to kill Chiara.

156
00:13:38,067 --> 00:13:39,360
What do you mean, Mom?

157
00:13:42,112 --> 00:13:44,448
I already have another option.

158
00:13:48,786 --> 00:13:49,620
One that

159
00:13:50,663 --> 00:13:51,789
will make sure

160
00:13:52,289 --> 00:13:54,959
they won't survive tonight.

161
00:14:03,342 --> 00:14:04,593
Sir.

162
00:14:09,974 --> 00:14:13,018
As far as I know,
she's connected to Chiara Valtrovi.

163
00:14:14,687 --> 00:14:17,022
That's how I got information from her.

164
00:14:17,982 --> 00:14:19,483
Chiara Valtrovi is here.

165
00:14:19,567 --> 00:14:22,152
And she's meeting Mikoy Pinagpala.

166
00:14:22,236 --> 00:14:24,738
So why is she giving us this information?

167
00:14:24,822 --> 00:14:26,740
She wants safe passage

168
00:14:27,241 --> 00:14:29,577
for her and her son, Rahmboy.

169
00:14:30,202 --> 00:14:32,663
It looks like the Concordat
is betraying Chiara.

170
00:14:33,914 --> 00:14:35,916
Chiara has a shoot-to-kill order.

171
00:14:36,417 --> 00:14:38,002
And if her information is accurate,

172
00:14:38,085 --> 00:14:39,587
then we can take her down.

173
00:14:41,005 --> 00:14:42,673
So, what about Mikoy?

174
00:14:43,465 --> 00:14:45,634
We won't be able to protect Mikoy anymore.

175
00:14:46,802 --> 00:14:49,763
If he's meeting with a known criminal,

176
00:14:50,306 --> 00:14:53,225
that makes him a legitimate target.

177
00:14:54,685 --> 00:14:57,855
We don't have any choice
but to take them both down.

178
00:15:01,108 --> 00:15:02,568
I'll prepare the team, sir.

179
00:15:38,896 --> 00:15:40,856
They want something in return.

180
00:16:11,804 --> 00:16:13,055
<i>I'm sorry, Dad.</i>

181
00:16:14,139 --> 00:16:15,766
<i>This is the only way I know.</i>

182
00:16:17,643 --> 00:16:19,186
<i>I'll do whatever it takes</i>

183
00:16:19,770 --> 00:16:22,106
<i>to make whoever did this pay.</i>

184
00:16:42,501 --> 00:16:44,294
<i>This is the life we have.</i>

185
00:16:45,212 --> 00:16:47,256
<i>This is the life that comes with power.</i>

186
00:16:51,844 --> 00:16:54,805
What if I were in that position?

187
00:16:54,888 --> 00:16:57,433
I cannot make a choice.

188
00:16:57,516 --> 00:17:00,352
Real happiness comes with real power.

189
00:17:00,436 --> 00:17:03,522
Being at the top,
where no one can bring you down.

190
00:17:04,023 --> 00:17:05,774
When we don't even have the right

191
00:17:05,858 --> 00:17:08,527
to decide our own lives.

192
00:17:10,404 --> 00:17:12,114
<i>We're already at the top.</i>

193
00:17:12,614 --> 00:17:14,324
<i>We have power.</i>

194
00:17:14,408 --> 00:17:16,577
<i>And I intend to keep that.</i>

195
00:17:17,578 --> 00:17:18,954
<i>Isn't there any other choice, Mom?</i>

196
00:17:20,664 --> 00:17:22,833
<i>Is this the only path forward?</i>

197
00:17:45,939 --> 00:17:46,940
This can't happen.

198
00:17:48,734 --> 00:17:50,360
I won't let this happen.

199
00:18:08,921 --> 00:18:10,130
Hello? Who is this?

200
00:18:10,839 --> 00:18:12,841
Brother Mikoy said
I should call this number

201
00:18:12,925 --> 00:18:13,884
if I ever needed anything.

202
00:18:14,468 --> 00:18:15,803
What do you need?

203
00:18:16,553 --> 00:18:18,889
This is all about Chiara and Mikoy.

204
00:18:20,849 --> 00:18:22,643
They need our help.

205
00:18:29,900 --> 00:18:32,611
- You know, I can't wait for the weekend.
- Bro.

206
00:18:32,694 --> 00:18:34,905
I'll definitely binge watch
my favorite series.

207
00:18:34,988 --> 00:18:36,490
For me, it's my K-dramas.

208
00:18:36,573 --> 00:18:37,699
I like that!

209
00:18:50,963 --> 00:18:51,797
Don’t move,

210
00:18:52,840 --> 00:18:54,341
or I'll shoot!

211
00:18:54,842 --> 00:18:55,843
Relax.

212
00:18:57,678 --> 00:18:58,554
I'm not your enemy.

213
00:19:00,264 --> 00:19:01,181
Don't say a word!

214
00:19:03,100 --> 00:19:04,434
What's going on here?

215
00:19:12,359 --> 00:19:14,069
Don't you recognize him?

216
00:19:19,658 --> 00:19:20,909
Lower your guns.

217
00:19:26,206 --> 00:19:28,208
He's Mikoy's secret asset.

218
00:19:32,462 --> 00:19:34,047
What is he doing here?

219
00:19:35,674 --> 00:19:36,925
Exactly.

220
00:19:37,009 --> 00:19:38,969
Weren't you supposed to be in Prague?

221
00:19:42,181 --> 00:19:44,641
I'm here to ask for your help.

222
00:19:45,809 --> 00:19:48,312
Mikoy and Chiara are in danger.

223
00:20:08,290 --> 00:20:09,458
ALEX

224
00:20:09,541 --> 00:20:10,918
This is Mikoy's, right?

225
00:20:14,254 --> 00:20:15,547
Mikoy, where are you?

226
00:20:16,715 --> 00:20:19,384
Oh, Agent Alex, it's Tess.

227
00:20:19,468 --> 00:20:21,637
<i>Mikoy left his phone here.</i>

228
00:20:22,930 --> 00:20:23,805
Is he there?

229
00:20:24,681 --> 00:20:25,933
Oh, do you want me to check outside?

230
00:20:26,016 --> 00:20:29,353
Yes, please. If he's there,
please tell him to call me right away.

231
00:20:29,436 --> 00:20:30,687
Okay, sure.

232
00:20:30,771 --> 00:20:32,731
Wait, Agent Alex. Is there a problem?

233
00:20:32,814 --> 00:20:35,692
No, nothing. I just have
something I want to ask him.

234
00:20:36,902 --> 00:20:37,778
Thank you.

235
00:20:39,988 --> 00:20:40,989
What?

236
00:20:41,698 --> 00:20:42,658
Did you talk to him?

237
00:20:46,620 --> 00:20:48,080
From what it looks like,

238
00:20:48,163 --> 00:20:50,832
he left behind the device
that can help us trace him.

239
00:21:28,287 --> 00:21:29,162
You?

240
00:21:29,246 --> 00:21:31,331
Tell me everything you know

241
00:21:31,415 --> 00:21:34,751
or I'll blow your head off
if anything happens to Mikoy.

242
00:21:35,377 --> 00:21:36,712
I can't give you an answer.

243
00:21:38,130 --> 00:21:39,631
This guy's crazy!

244
00:21:41,174 --> 00:21:44,261
But I can take you to someone
who knows where they are.

245
00:21:45,512 --> 00:21:46,513
Who?

246
00:21:47,889 --> 00:21:49,141
My very own mother.

247
00:21:50,559 --> 00:21:52,185
Vicky Corales.

248
00:21:53,645 --> 00:21:54,730
The one that hailed as

249
00:21:56,064 --> 00:21:57,232
the Widow's Maid.

250
00:22:10,829 --> 00:22:13,623
But my sense tells me
that I should trust you.

251
00:22:14,458 --> 00:22:16,752
Just like the trust Mikoy has in you.

252
00:23:19,606 --> 00:23:23,860
The tracker I planted on you, Chiara,
has finally been activated.

253
00:24:01,773 --> 00:24:04,818
Looks like my sweetheart
still hasn't changed at all.

254
00:24:08,405 --> 00:24:12,492
If I didn't know you,
I'd think you're still that waiter

255
00:24:14,953 --> 00:24:17,998
who works at that cute little café

256
00:24:18,915 --> 00:24:20,333
by the Vltava River.

257
00:24:43,440 --> 00:24:44,733
I loved you

258
00:24:44,816 --> 00:24:46,359
without any conditions.

259
00:24:46,860 --> 00:24:48,945
Then you killed Dad.

260
00:24:50,572 --> 00:24:52,365
<i>Where is Mikoy and Chiara, huh?</i>

261
00:24:53,408 --> 00:24:54,784
Agent Alex, please.

262
00:24:54,868 --> 00:24:56,411
But I don’t have enought time.

263
00:24:56,494 --> 00:24:59,956
At this point, Mikoy and Chiara
are probably dead.

264
00:25:00,040 --> 00:25:01,666
I already talked to Agent Dara.

265
00:25:09,841 --> 00:25:12,719
I'll use this to make you feel

266
00:25:12,802 --> 00:25:14,512
what you did to my father.

267
00:25:33,114 --> 00:25:34,115
